# Norin, Swift Survivalist: the exile is a "may". In turn 3 Bot1 declines it for its blocked Runeclaw Bear, which then kills the
# 0/2 Ornithopter that blocked it. In turn 4 Bot2's Runeclaw Bear attacks: Norin "can't block" (CR 509.1b), so a block by him is refused,
# while Bot1's untapped Ornithopter may block it, and no question is asked (Bot2's attacker is not "a creature you control", and
# Bot1's blocker blocks rather than becomes blocked): the Ornithopter dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Norin, Swift Survivalist
Runeclaw Bear
Ornithopter
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Runeclaw Bear
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Norin, Swift Survivalist.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Runeclaw Bear.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Runeclaw Bear.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Runeclaw Bear > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Runeclaw Bear)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Decline
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
? Exile = 
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Runeclaw Bear > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Norin, Swift Survivalist > Runeclaw Bear)
Bot1.Block(Ornithopter > Runeclaw Bear)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
